  "title": "Builder-family detection, fail-closed reviews, and diff-aware posting",
  "summary": "This change makes the review pipeline stricter and more forgiving at once. Builder-family detection now reads every word of a `Code-Generator:` trailer (vendor names and model ids alike) instead of only the first, and a clean merge with no trailer is exempt via a new `git merge-tree` check. When any commit leaves the builder family unknown, the run now fails closed: no reviewer counts, the outcome is could-not-run, and the reason quotes the offending trailer. Reviewers skipped for sharing the builder's family record why in their saved run and in the posted summary. Finally, review posting fetches the PR diff and only anchors inline comments on lines the diff actually shows; findings outside it go into the body, which is now cut to its limit and counts what did not fit rather than refusing to post.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
